                                       <h1 style="color: #0d47a1; font-size: 30px;"><strong>How to Download Your NISM Series V-A Certificate After Passing?</strong></h1>
                      
                                        <p class="about-text" style="color:#000; text-align:justify; margin-top:20px;">
After successfully clearing the NISM Series V-A Mutual Fund Distributors Certification Exam, candidates can download their official certificate from the NISM certification portal.
<br><br>
The certificate is issued by National Institute of Securities Markets under the regulatory framework of 
<a href="https://www.sebi.gov.in/" target="_blank" style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;">
Securities and Exchange Board of India.
</a>
<br><br>
This certification is an important professional credential for individuals who want to work as mutual fund distributors, financial advisors, relationship managers, or wealth management professionals. It confirms that the candidate has successfully completed the required certification and understands the regulatory and operational aspects of mutual fund distribution.
<br><br>
Once the exam result is declared, candidates can download their certificate directly from the candidate dashboard.
</p>


<h2 class="mt-5" style="color:#0d47a1; font-size:28px;">Steps to Download the NISM Series V-A Certificate</h2>

<!-- Infographic -->
<div style="text-align:center; margin-top:25px; margin-bottom:25px;">
    <img src="../../images/HowTo/Download the NISM Series V-A Certificate.png"
         alt="Download the NISM Series V-A Certificate Infographic"
         style="max-width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
</div>



<ul style="list-style:none; padding-left:0; color:#000; margin-top:20px;">

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> Visit the certification portal of 
<a href="https://certifications.nism.ac.in" target="_blank" style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;">
National Institute of Securities Markets
</a>.
</li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> Log in to your candidate account using your registered email ID and password.</li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> After logging in, open the <strong>Candidate Dashboard</strong>.</li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> Navigate to the section <strong>“My Certifications”</strong> or <strong>“My Enrolments.”</strong></li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> Locate the certification <strong>Mutual Fund Distributors Certification (Series V-A)</strong>.</li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> Click on <strong>“View Details.”</strong></li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> Look for the option <strong>“Download Certificate.”</strong></li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> Click the download button to open the certificate.</li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> The certificate will be available in <strong>PDF format</strong>.</li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> Download and save the file for your records.</li>

<li><span style="color:#0d47a1; font-weight:bold;">✔</span> You may also print the certificate for professional or compliance purposes.</li>

</ul>


<h2 class="mt-5" style="color:#0d47a1; font-size:28px;">Conclusion</h2>

<p class="about-text" style="color:#000; text-align:justify; margin-top:20px;">
Downloading the NISM Series V-A Mutual Fund Distributors certificate is a simple process through the candidate dashboard on the certification portal of the National Institute of Securities Markets.
<br><br>
Once downloaded, candidates should keep both digital and printed copies of the certificate for future reference. The certification serves as official proof of qualification and helps professionals meet the regulatory requirements established by Securities and Exchange Board of India for mutual fund distributors in India.
</p>                                     
